class_name EffectPoolHashes
extends RefCounted
## The effect pool's hash over every frame of each trace scenario (`EffectPoolHash`), taken from the code as it
## stood before `EffectObjects` and `ArcadeEffectObjects` shared their helpers. A scenario missing from a
## table fails as "expected -1"; a failure prints the hash in decimal and the tables hold it in hex
## (`"%x" % value`), so a deliberate change of the pool is taken over by copying it in that form.
## TODO: object types the scenarios never reach are not covered: the PlayStation's Gon flame (8), floor fire
## (9), Ball glow (15) and gas (19, 20), the arcade's ember (5), cloud (10) and power sparks (12, 13). A
## scenario that reaches them (count `o.type` over `pool.objects` per frame to find one) would let their
## update functions be merged under the same guard.

